finding: Gate is green (189 tests), but it does not enforce stage 4's placement claim. 1. scripts/check-example-ui.node.ts:625-641 detects position only on an identical selector and checks only top/right/bottom/left. Independent probes through the unchanged controlViolations function return [] for `.hint {position:absolute} .hint[hidden] {bottom:24px}` and `.hint {position:absolute;inset:24px}`. Both allow viewport-edge placement with no safe-area offset. The latter is not the permitted full-parent inset:0 surface. DOM style property assignments and Svelte style: directives are also unread (lines 62-65, 90-109, 116-159): probes of `button.style.position='absolute';button.style.bottom='24px'` and `<button style:position={'absolute'} style:bottom={'24px'}>Jump</button>` likewise return no violations. New controls need not use the specially recognized player.ts/cssText spelling to be subject to the rule. 2. scripts/check-example-ui.node.ts:625-641 has no containing-block/owner distinction. `.reticle {position:absolute;top:0;left:0}` returns two safe-area violations even when positioned inside a non-viewport owner; `.reticle {position:absolute;top:25%;left:25%}` also returns two. Explicit four-side zero full-parent surfaces are similarly rejected, while inset:0 passes. Only the literal 50% and a couple of calc prefixes are exempt, not owner-relative positioning. This forbids legitimate layouts and can force double safe-area padding inside an already inset owner. Independent checks: baseline gate 189 passed; scratch-only copy of gate with added diagnostic probes (no worktree source edits); first-person touch browser subject 3 passed, minimap touch 1 passed, view-model touch 2 passed. Read the unit Premise/stage 4, example-controls specification, CONTRIBUTING, commit diff, discovery/parser and placement logic; inspected embedded-scene and save-and-load sizing changes. No demonstrated layout regression in those two pages; svh/dvh probes pass. Existing touch owners' cssText offsets were updated, and no additional currently mounted owner was demonstrated missing. Remaining uncertainty: no iPhone/Safari device pass and no browser layout comparison of embedded-scene/save-and-load. The new negative placement tests can fail on the old gate; the positive exemption case passing before the fix is not itself a defect.
